WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:52.700
This is the law. You obey it or else. That is the basis. He says, you do it or else. That is the vision. Then there is a more sophisticated approach. Judaism does not believe in neither of these ideas.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.580
He reveals himself in Mount Sinai.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.140
And he says, listen, I have a deal for you.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.180
We're going to study it. We're going to read it.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.040
The deal is as follows.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.020
I have certain sects or rules.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.640
If you accept them,

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.620
then you accept my laws,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.100
and you live by those laws,

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.780
then I'm going to protect you,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.720
and I'm going to take care of you.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:39.040
It is an alliance. It is a covenant. It is a mutually agreed upon covenant. And therefore, in Harsinai, the law is presented. Do you want it? Yes or no? It's up to you.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.320
we accepted it, we sealed the covenant,

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.220
and therefore it becomes the law because we said,

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:51.740
We accepted it.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:57.260
And we become God's chosen people because we chose to be his people.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.200
And therefore God will protect us in a special manner

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.120
and will bestow upon us certain special graces

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.760
because we accept it out of our free choice.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:13.480
It's Tora.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.440
What do we say?

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.220
أَشَرْ بَحَارْ بَعْنُو

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.620
مِنْ كُلْهَا عَمِيمٌ

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.740
God chose us.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.220
It's a question of choosing.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.800
The best example,

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.440
if you want to understand this kind of relationship,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.320
is that of a wife and a husband.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.100
You don't have to marry this man.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.620
He doesn't have to marry this woman.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.660
Both together they make a belief, they make a covenant.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:47.260
And because they make a covenant between themselves, there are certain stipulations, rules,

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.920
reglamenting the lives.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.740
Before you were married, you could choose to do anything you want.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:03:01.880
But if you marry and you accept this covenant, this alliance,

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.280
simply because

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.820
you have accepted

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.100
a set of rules.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.060
This is the

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.740
parasha today.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.320
Now there are two aspects, two parts to the parasha.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.360
One that we are not going to read

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.740
Harry got that correctly, says

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.640
there is a story and so on. Let's go

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.020
into the meat and potatoes

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.200
of the parasha. But let me nonetheless

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.360
mention about it.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.200
This is about Yitro.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.000
Yitro is

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.940
Hoten Moshe.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.120
Hoten Moshe

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.200
is poorly translated as

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.780
the father-in-law of Moses.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.200
It is not true.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.840
It was not his father-in-law.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:44.360
As a matter of fact,

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.780
the parasha in Shemotz is very clear

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.840
that Zipporah was the daughter of Re'uel.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.440
So who was Hoten?

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.900
Hoten is something very similar

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.200
to an Ashkenaz or an Yiddish word.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:03:59.600
Mechusen.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:00.520
Conference?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:05.080
Anybody who is related to you through marriage,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.680
be it father-in-law, son-in-law, brother-in-law,

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.280
a nephew-in-law.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.980
So, Yitron truly was the brother-in-law of Moshe Rabbenu.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.800
And he's called Oden,

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.760
because he became his relation through Hakunah.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.120
You understand?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.440
Now, something extraordinary.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:41.440
The most important parasha in the Tora. The Ten Commandments, Mount Sinai. The name of the parasha is that of a gentile, Yitro.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:52.440
Now, you have to understand the strategy of the Tora, the literary strategy of the Tora. How does it finish, the last parasha?

00:04:52.440 --> 00:05:06.600
We leave Egypt, we cross the Red Sea, miracles witnessed by everybody, we're going minding

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:12.760
our own business, going to the Holy Land, after to Sinai, and all of a sudden there's

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:19.440
a group of people called Amalek that attack us in a merciless, cruel way.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.300
This is the first act of terrorism registered in human history.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.300
Alright?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.300
Fine.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:30.200
The next perasha begins with Yitro.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.200
Yitro was a gentile.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:37.880
Nonetheless, although he was a gentile, he was a good man.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:40.360
What the Tora is teaching us here?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.360
It is teaching us something, two things which are very important.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.060
Number one, it is true.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:53.840
are goyim that are like Amalek. No question about this. Alright. But at the same time

00:05:53.840 --> 00:06:02.560
that there are goyim who are like Amalek, they are individual people like Yitro.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:12.020
It's number one. Number two, the same thing said in different words. What may be good

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:20.420
is never a people. Don't trust a nation, the French nation, the Russian nation, the German

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:29.720
nation, the Spanish nation. As a nation you cannot trust them, the British, etc. So therefore what

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:38.300
there may be good is not as a nation of Midian, but an individual person by the name of Yitro.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.800
don't confuse an individual

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.200
with his nation

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.900
nations we cannot trust

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.120
Jews who put their trust

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:47.860
in nations

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.620
did not have a happy ending

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:53.080
we could see that

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.580
there are some good individuals

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.460
and we respect them

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.080
and we're going to cherish them

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.320
and we're going to applaud them

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.400
and in Israel they have a special

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.880
award for Hasidic

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.700
for those gentiles

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.620
who show extraordinary valor

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.880
and we applaud them and we love them.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.160
But those are individuals.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:15.540
Alright?

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:20.200
Now comes the most important

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.560
question.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:23.980
290.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:25.360
Alright?

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.380
In the third month,

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:41.500
The story begins three months after 290.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:42.120
Yes?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.060
Yes, at the bottom.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:49.820
Three months after, in the third month after leaving Egypt.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.960
Not three months after, but in the third month.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.180
Which is, is minus 49 days yet.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:57.620
Because the 49, the 50 days is going to be Matan Tora.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.600
This is three days before Matan Tora.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.460
Now, very important, it doesn't give you the name of the month.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:05.660
Alright?

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:07.080
It says,

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:12.480
Here again we come to something very, very important.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.340
Dates, for us, are meaningless.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:19.600
It doesn't mean anything.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:26.380
A lot of people who believe in astrology, good day, bad day, this is nonsense.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:35.380
What makes this day important is not that what month it is, the third month, the fifth month.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:45.380
What is important is the historical context in which it is.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:55.380
This is an important event because it takes place as a consequence of another historical event,

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.920
the exodus from Egypt. Do you understand the accent? The accent is,

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:10.700
It is that historical event that will make this event meaningful. Correct?

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.640
And what is the lesson? It's very simple. Before, what did we acquire?

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:20.780
Physical freedom. Bondage from physical slavery.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:30.780
What are we going to acquire now? Spiritual, individual freedom. The freedom that is awarded through the law and the covenant with God.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:32.780
Alright?

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:45.460
In that very day, the Jewish people entered into the desert of Sinai.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.920
And they left a place called Repidim.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.240
And they camped in the desert.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:08.020
And the Jewish people there, they camp facing the mountain.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:12.420
And the mountain, the mountain, is of course Mount Sinai.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.340
Now, it's interesting things.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.140
Look in the Settah pasuq.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.620
Plural.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.220
Plural.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:23.600
Plural.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:31.400
Tora is given a very important

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:36.020
before the Jewish people

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.200
accepted the Tora

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.760
before they made the covenant

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:42.360
there was a need

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.000
to become

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.040
a single unit

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.040
the Jewish people achieved what we call in Hebrew

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.560
Ahdut, internal unity

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.800
Vayih Han A'am

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:53.980
negative.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:55.200
Yes.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.660
It is become

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.220
a single entity.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:04.760
One minute.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.380
I talk about the Tabha Hamim.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.860
One of the Tabha Hamim died

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.500
1900.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:12.680
Rabi Yahweh and Amozek.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.980
Here's an extraordinary question. He says,

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.260
why is it important to have unity

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.780
before the Tora?

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.400
Before receiving the Tora.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:26.780
Why can't we have unity as a result of accepting the Tora?

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.440
Why does there have to be a condition before?

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:33.220
Unless you have united, God will not give you the Tora.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:35.400
No, he will say, listen, we're not united,

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.260
but because of the Tora we can be united.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.320
This is something very important.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:39.160
Listen to this.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.180
And this pertains to our own situation as truth today.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.560
If we are united,

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.860
and we share this selfishness,

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:56.620
egotism, jealousy against other people,

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.180
then the Tora could be meaningful.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.320
But if we are selfish,

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.100
and each one is separated from the other,

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:06.960
sees competition with the other,

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:08.460
and hateful to that,

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:09.620
you know what would happen?

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:10.720
You would take the Tora

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:16.100
and use it to promote your own hatred against other Jews.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.720
As unfortunately sometimes it does happen.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:43.000
So that's why God wanted us first to forget and forgive, become united. Then we accepted the Tora and that the Tora could help us. But if we are not united, the Tora is going to turn into an instrument for attacking one another.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:47.960
I will never forget several years ago I went to Argentina and somebody was in the

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:52.360
Kmeez and somebody asked me about the brand of a cheese. I never heard this brand of a cheese.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:56.000
I just saw some Argentinian kosher cheese. He says, is it kasher or not kasher?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:02.160
I said, I don't know. So well, you know, really this Hakam said that if you eat this cheese you have no

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.520
hirah rabba. And people say, what do you mean you have no hirah rabba? Yes you have hirah rabba.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:10.440
So I said, do you know what I mean? Kosher cheese now becomes a means to divide Jews?

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:13.300
He should be the United Jews, you know.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:16.400
So it becomes, yeah, no, that's not God's question.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.900
That's the real God's question.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:24.200
Therefore Judaism becomes, the Tora becomes an instrument for attacking and hatred.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.200
But now we understand why.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.700
vayih han ha'am neged ha'ar.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:32.700
U'moshe alayh el-elohim.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:36.200
And Moses goes up to God,

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:40.200
Vayiqra elav Adonai min ha'ar lemort,

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:44.200
and God calls or summons Moshe saying,

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:45.700
Kortuman lev et Yaaqob,

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.200
thus you shall speak to the house of Jacob,

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:50.200
et aged lemne Yisrael,

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.200
you shall speak to the sons of Israel.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:56.200
It's a very awkward pasuq. Very, very awkward.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.200
It says, what it says,

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:02.200
V'ya'al Moshe elah Elohim.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.200
Moses goes up to God,

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.200
and then, V'ikra'elav Elohim,

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.200
and then God calls him.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.200
That should be the other way around.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.200
God calls Moses,

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:17.200
V'ikra'elohim et Moshe,

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:20.200
and then should be, V'ya'al Moshe elah Elohim.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:23.180
talking about

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:30.360
generation after the

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:34.720
God will not

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.020
reveal himself to you

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.860
unless you make

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:39.940
the first move

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:47.040
Moses makes the first move

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:49.380
he tried to go up

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:53.320
He tried to come up to God, and therefore,

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:56.680
And therefore God calls him.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:01.780
But if you're waiting for God to call you, you could wait all your life.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:03.220
He will not call you.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:06.000
You make the first step.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:06.820
Clear?

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:08.880
Very clear, no?

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:09.580
To the point.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:10.240
Alright?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:11.100
So now,

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:21.580
Now God is going to have a mission for him.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.980
Thus you shall speak to the household of Jacob.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.320
The rabbis say that this refers to the women.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:40.160
And thereafter, he's going to say to the sons of Israel.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:58.100
Now, of course, why first women? Alright. There are two reasons. One which is a humorous one. It says, God says, I learned my lesson. I learned my lesson.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:05.100
When Adam and Eve were in the Garden of Eden, what did I do?

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:12.100
I told Adam the law, and Eve went and subverted everything, and he went against the law.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:20.100
I learned my lesson, God says, now I'm going to say first to the women, let them agree, and then I'm going to tell to the men.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:25.100
Do you know who says this? Ribbi Isaac Karo, the uncle of Maran Akadosh.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:28.180
That's why he says that. But then there is another reason.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.900
It's very important. The question of democracy.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.900
See, we're talking a society in which, of course, the woman was

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:41.180
serving to the husband. Now, if she,

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.360
if God would have spoken first to the man,

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:48.140
then the woman would not have dared say no.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.600
So now God speaks first to the woman.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:17:01.680
No coercion, the Haithams are not present, they did not express an opinion, you're free

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:11.980
either to accept or reject. And therefore, first you go and you speak to the women, you tell them

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:19.280
what the proposal is, and then they tagge the name Israel. Because both parties, they have to agree,

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:24.500
and they have to agree without any kind of even psychological coercion.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:25.140
You understand?

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:31.480
Again, if you say first to the women and the men say yes, then it goes to the women,

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.920
many of them, they will not dare contradict their husband.

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:40.320
God gives them an opportunity for them to say no.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:41.320
Clear?

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:42.840
All right?

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:43.440
Fine.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:48.500
Now we're going to see what the deal is.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:49.580
Alright?

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:52.580
That was also from Yishaq Karo?

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:53.660
No.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.460
Atem reitem

00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:59.340
et asher asit

00:17:59.340 --> 00:17:59.960
ilim Yisrael.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:01.520
Now on second.

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.300
You have experienced

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.080
what I have done

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.060
in Egypt.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:10.900
If I ask

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.300
again, a member of

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:14.760
any religion except Judaism,

